# Campus Köthen — assessed vulnerability exceptions for the published images.
#
# This file is NOT a place to quiet inconvenient findings. Every entry states
# what was checked, why the finding does not apply, and what keeps it from
# silently becoming real again. Anything not listed here fails the build.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-14257 — brace-expansion: DoS via unbounded expansion length
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reported against `brace-expansion 1.1.18` in the CMS image.
#
# Why it does not apply: the advisory publishes ONE major-spanning range
# ("<=5.0.7 vulnerable, >=5.0.8 fixed"), so it still matches the BACKPORTED
# releases on the 1.x and 2.x lines. The fix is demonstrably present in what we
# ship — 1.1.18 introduces EXPANSION_MAX_LENGTH plus the bounding check
# `if (length + expansion.length > maxLength) return out`, and its source
# comment names this very CVE.
#
# Why we do not simply upgrade to 5.x: v5 is an ESM-first rewrite whose
# CommonJS entry exports `{ expand }` instead of the function itself. The
# consumer here is `minimatch@3`, deep inside Strapi's own tree
# (@strapi/strapi -> fork-ts-checker-webpack-plugin -> minimatch@3), and it
# calls the default export directly — verified by requiring the built package,
# which yields an object, not a callable. Forcing the major would turn a
# scanner warning into a real runtime failure.
#
# What keeps this honest: pnpm-workspace.yaml pins every affected major line to
# its patched minimum (>=1.1.17, >=2.1.3, >=5.0.8), so a genuinely vulnerable
# version cannot come back unnoticed. Re-check whenever the advisory range is
# corrected upstream or Strapi drops minimatch@3.
CVE-2026-14257
